<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-25">25 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Louise Brown, the first 'test-tube baby', is born</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Louise Brown was born in Oldham, the first person conceived by in vitro fertilisation, pioneered by Robert Edwards and Patrick Steptoe. Millions of people have since been born through IVF.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-26">26 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Albino Luciani is elected Pope John Paul I</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> became the first pope to take a double name, honouring his two predecessors. Known as the 'smiling pope', he died after just 33 days.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-17">17 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Egypt and Israel sign the Camp David Accords</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After 13 days of talks hosted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jimmy-carter">Jimmy Carter</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anwar-sadat">Anwar Sadat</a> and Menachem Begin signed two frameworks for peace. They led to the Egypt-Israel peace treaty of March 1979.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-27">27 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mayor Moscone and Harvey Milk are shot in San Francisco</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Former supervisor Dan White shot dead Mayor George Moscone and Supervisor Harvey Milk at City Hall. Milk had been one of the first openly gay elected officials in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/saur-revolution" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saur-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolution</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/saur-revolution">Saur Revolution</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Saur Revolution was the coup of 27–28 April 1978 in which army units loyal to the People's Democratic Party of Afghanistan overthrew and killed President Mohammad Daoud Khan.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/third-plenum-of-the-11th-central-committee">Third Plenum of the 11th Central Committee</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Third Plenum of the 11th Central Committee of the Chinese Communist Party, held in Beijing in December 1978, confirmed Deng Xiaoping as China's leading figure.</p></div></li></ol></section>
